 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+A session is a cookie: the member and the session's expiry, signed with HMAC-SHA256 under `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`
+([keep sessions in signed cookies](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md)). `verify` in
+`larder/sessions.py` returns the member, or none when the signature does not match or the expiry has passed. Every
+web server holds the same key, so any server accepts the cookie and a deploy logs no one out.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- A session cannot be ended from the server before it expires. The only workaround is to rotate
+  `LARDER_SESSION_KEY`, which logs every member out, so do it only between pickups.
 
